\title{ecoPortfolio: Climate Risk Metrics for Equity Portfolios}
\description{
Calculates the carbon metrics recommended for portfolio disclosure by the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) and the International Sustainability Standards Board (ISSB): weighted average carbon intensity (WACI), financed emissions attributed by enterprise value including cash as in the Partnership for Carbon Accounting Financials (PCAF) standard, and carbon footprint. Also reports data coverage, decomposes the WACI gap to a benchmark into sector allocation and stock selection effects, and runs carbon price stress tests that translate scenario paths into earnings at risk and valuation shocks. Metrics work on emissions data you supply; optional helpers download asset-level emissions and owners from the open Climate TRACE API \url{https://climatetrace.org} and match owners to holdings by normalised company name.
}
\section{Getting started}{

Put holdings in standard form with \code{\link[=climate_portfolio]{climate_portfolio()}}, then compute
\code{\link[=waci]{waci()}}, \code{\link[=financed_emissions]{financed_emissions()}} and \code{\link[=carbon_footprint]{carbon_footprint()}} (or all at once
with \code{\link[=climate_metrics]{climate_metrics()}}), check \code{\link[=data_coverage]{data_coverage()}}, compare with a
benchmark using \code{\link[=compare_benchmark]{compare_benchmark()}} and \code{\link[=waci_attribution]{waci_attribution()}}, and run
\code{\link[=carbon_stress_test]{carbon_stress_test()}}. Emissions can come from your own data or from
Climate TRACE via \code{\link[=ct_assets]{ct_assets()}}, \code{\link[=owner_emissions]{owner_emissions()}} and
\code{\link[=match_holdings]{match_holdings()}}.
}

